            0.059
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "organic evolution-prehistory"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.085,
            0.5,
            0.144
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "organic evolution the principle set forth by Darwin that every plant or animal has evolved, or changed, over a long period of time from earlier, simpler forms of life to more complex forms (p. 608)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.144,
            0.497,
            0.161
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "orthodoxy traditional beliefs, especially in religion (p. 469)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.162,
            0.499,
            0.206
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "ostracism in ancient Athens, the process for temporarily banning ambitious politicians from the city by popular vote (p. 123)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.206,
            0.5,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "ozone layer a thin layer of gas in the upper atmosphere that shields Earth from the sun's ultraviolet rays (p. 970)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.295,
            0.269,
            0.313,
            0.286
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "P"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.297,
            0.501,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Paleolithic Age from the Greek for \"Old Stone,\" the early period of human history, from approximately 2,500,000 to 10,000 B.C., during which humans used simple stone tools; sometimes called the Old Stone Age (p. 22)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.372,
            0.501,
            0.402
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pan-Africanism the unity of all black Africans, regardless of national boundaries (pp. 788, 923)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.403,
            0.499,
            0.433
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pan-Arabism Arab unity, regardless of national boundaries (p. 931)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.434,
            0.461,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "partisan a resistance fighter in World War II (p. 822)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.451,
            0.5,
            0.496
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "pasha an appointed official in the Ottoman Empire who collected taxes, maintained law and order, and was directly responsible to the sultan's court (p. 459)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.496,
            0.5,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "pastoral nomad a person who domesticates animals for food and clothing and moves along regular migratory routes to provide a steady source of nourishment for those animals (p. 55)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.555,
            0.5,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "paterfamilias in the Roman social structure, the dominant male head of the household, which also included his wife, sons and their wives and children, unmarried daughters, and slaves (p. 165)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.613,
            0.499,
            0.645
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "patriarch the head of the Eastern Orthodox Church, originally appointed by the Byzantine emperor (p. 305)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.645,
            0.362,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "patriarchal dominated by men (p. 41)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.662,
            0.499,
            0.692
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "patrician great landowners, they formed the ruling class in the Roman Republic (p. 152)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.692,
            0.465,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "patrilineal tracing lineage through the father (p. 237)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.71,
            0.499,
            0.754
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "peacekeeping force a military force drawn from neutral members of the United Nations to settle conflicts and supervise truces (p. 975)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.104,
            0.755,
            0.5,
            0.813
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "peninsular a person born on the Iberian Peninsula; typically, a Spanish or Portuguese official who resided temporarily in Latin America for political and economic gain and then returned to Europe (p. 672)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.814,
            0.308,
            0.831
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "per capita per person (p. 943)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.831,
            0.499,
            0.862
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "perestroika Mikhail Gorbachev's plan to reform the Soviet Union by restructuring its economy (p. 877)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.863,
            0.501,
            0.921
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "permanent revolution an atmosphere of constant revolutionary fervor favored by Mao Zedong to enable China to overcome the past and achieve the final stage of communism (p. 942)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.521,
            0.085,
            0.917,
            0.116
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "phalanx a wall of shields created by foot soldiers marching close together in a rectangular formation (p. 116)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.521,
            0.117,
            0.918,
            0.161
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "pharaoh the most common of the various titles for ancient Egyptian monarchs; the term originally meant “great house” or “palace” (p. 47)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.161,
            0.916,
            0.206
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "philosophe French for \"philosopher\"; applied to all intellectuals—i.e., writers, journalists, economists, and social reformers—during the Enlightenment (p. 519)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.206,
            0.916,
            0.236
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "philosophy an organized system of thought, from the Greek for \"love of wisdom\" (p. 130)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.238,
            0.916,
            0.269
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "photomontage a picture made of a combination of photographs (p. 774)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 27,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.269,
            0.916,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "pilgrim a person who travels to a shrine or other holy place (p. 85)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 28,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.3,
            0.768,
            0.316
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "plague an epidemic disease (p. 176)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 29,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.317,
            0.916,
            0.347
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "planned economy an economic system directed by government agencies (p. 726)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 30,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.347,
            0.825,
            0.365
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "plantation a large agricultural estate (p. 416)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 31,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.365,
            0.842,
            0.381
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "plateau a relatively high, flat land area (p. 225)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 32,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.382,
            0.916,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "plebeian in the Roman Republic, a social class made up of minor landholders, craftspeople, merchants, and small farmers (p. 152)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 33,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.426,
            0.749,
            0.444
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "plebiscite a popular vote (p. 600)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 34,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.445,
            0.916,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "pogrom organized persecution or massacre of a minority group, especially Jews (p. 639)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 35,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.475,
            0.917,
            0.519
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "policy of containment a plan to keep something, such as communism, within its existing geographical boundaries and prevent further aggressive moves (p. 850)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 36,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.52,
            0.916,
            0.549
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "polis the early Greek city-state, consisting of a city or town and its surrounding territory (p. 115)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 37,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.55,
            0.917,
            0.594
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Politburo a seven-member committee that became the leading policy-making body of the Communist Party in Russia (p. 761)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 38,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.595,
            0.781,
            0.612
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "polytheistic having many gods (p. 42)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 39,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.613,
            0.917,
            0.657
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "pop art an artistic movement that emerged in the early 1960s; pop artists took images from popular culture and transformed them into works of fine art (p. 892)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 40,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.657,
            0.916,
            0.687
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "pope the bishop of Rome and head of the Roman Catholic Church (p. 287)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 41,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.688,
            0.916,
            0.719
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "porcelain a ceramic made of fine clay baked at very high temperatures (pp. 257, 494)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 42,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.72,
            0.917,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "postmodernism an artistic movement that emerged in the 1980s; it is characterized by a revival of traditional elements and techniques, and includes crafts such as textiles, pottery, and furniture making in addition to traditional artistic media (p. 893)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 43,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.792,
            0.917,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "praetor an official of the Roman Republic in charge of enforcing civil law (p. 152)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 44,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.823,
            0.916,
            0.868
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "predestination the belief that God has determined in advance who will be saved (the elect) and who will be damned (the reprobate) (p. 396)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 45,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.869,
            0.915,
            0.898
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "prefecture in the Japanese Meiji Restoration, a territory governed by its former daimyo lord (p. 699)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 46,
          "bbox": [
            0.522,
            0.899,
            0.915,
            0.917
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "prehistory the period before writing was developed (p. 19)"
            }
          ]
        },
